SITREP 01
Reporting body: West Mercia Local Resilience Forum
Time of report: 27/01/2026 07:00
Reporting officer: Priya Raman, Duty Resilience Officer

SITUATION
Persistent heavy rainfall across the Leadon catchment overnight. River Leadon
has overtopped its banks at Ledbury. Environment Agency flood warning in force
for Ledbury and Leadon Valley since 0430.

IMPACTS
- 12 residential properties confirmed flooded, Bye Street and Woodleigh Road,=
 Ledbury
- Approx 40 residents evacuated
- Rest centre opened 0600 at Ledbury Community Hall, HR8 2AA, capacity 80
- A417 closed in both directions between Ledbury and Gloucester Road junction
- One primary school closed (St Michael's Primary School, Ledbury)

RESOURCES
Hereford and Worcester Fire and Rescue Service: 3 pumps, 1 boat team on scene.
West Mercia Police managing cordon.

FORWARD LOOK
Further 15-25mm rainfall forecast. Peak river levels expected late morning.

Next SITREP 27/01/2026 13:00.
